MANUAL CONVERSION RULES APPLIED:
=================================
1. All table names converted to lowercase (Products->products, ProductHistory->producthistory, ProductStats->productstats)
2. All column names converted to lowercase per DMS schema mapping
3. SCOPE_IDENTITY() -> lastval() (PostgreSQL equivalent for last generated identity value)
4. GETDATE() -> NOW() (PostgreSQL equivalent for current timestamp)
5. BEGIN TRANSACTION -> BEGIN (PostgreSQL transaction syntax)
6. DECLARE @var / SET @var = ... -> Replaced with subqueries/CTEs where possible for ADO.NET compatibility
7. CTE name 'ProductStats' renamed to 'productstats_cte' to avoid conflict with table name 'productstats'
8. CTE name 'ProductHistory' renamed to 'producthistory_cte' to avoid conflict with table name 'producthistory'
9. Integer division in ROUND() wrapped with CAST(... AS numeric) for proper decimal division in PostgreSQL
10. Transaction statement ordering adjusted in Delete to capture values before deletion

